<PageLayout
  title="Gentle Yoga Teacher Training"
  lead="Continuing education for yoga teachers — learn to make yoga accessible to all types of students."
  description="Gentle Yoga Teacher Training (Yoga Alliance continuing education) at the Toronto Sivananda Yoga Vedanta Centre."
  narrow
>
  <Prose>
    <p>
      Gentle or accessible yoga is an approach in which all muscle groups are worked individually,
      allowing each posture to be comfortable while still balanced, strengthening and stretching,
      and allowing for relaxation. With this method, any student can safely follow the program and
      experience the benefits. Students don't need to adapt to yoga — yoga is flexible enough for
      everyone.
    </p>
    <p>
      This training focuses on how to make yoga practice available to all types of students: those
      with different fitness levels, starting a practice later in life or new to yoga, students with
      injuries or mobility difficulties, students who are overweight or pregnant, those suffering
      from anxiety, and more. It counts as a 12-hour Continued Education Certification with Yoga
      Alliance and is open to yoga teachers of all traditions.
    </p>

    <h2>Program outline</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Simple and profound postures; how to adapt the 12 basic asanas.</li>
      <li>How to sequence a class; teaching methods.</li>
      <li>Strength or flexibility? Teaching a mixed-level class.</li>
      <li>Philosophy of gentle yoga; classical yoga philosophy.</li>
      <li>How to modify postures for those who cannot reach the floor.</li>
      <li>Working with injuries; contraindications.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Course dates are announced through the year — please check upcoming events or contact us.</p>

    <h2>Your teacher</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Anjaneya (Michael Hutkins)</strong> teaches traditional Hatha Yoga and meditation to students
      of all ages and abilities. Teaching in his own studio as well as for many Sivananda Centres and
      Ashrams, he specializes in training yoga teachers in Chair and Gentle Yoga, helping to make yoga
      more accessible. All programs are based on his foundation of classical Hatha Yoga in the Sivananda
      lineage.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</PageLayout>
